Temporary local validation patch for SGLang PR #48969 (NOT for upstream)

Purpose: extend the grouped decode-attention launch-config gate so that exactly
gfx1100 (AMD Radeon PRO W7900, RDNA3.0) is additionally accepted, enabling an
independent A/B measurement of the PR's launch optimization on RDNA3.0 as
requested in PR #48969 (issuecomment-6703266031).

Scope guarantees:
- gfx115x (gfx1150/gfx1151/...) behavior is bit-identical: is_gfx115_supported()
  keeps its original semantics and is still evaluated first.
- Only the exact gfx1100 SKU prefix is accepted; gfx1101/gfx1102/gfx1103 and all
  other architectures remain excluded.
- No change to the reported GPU architecture, tensor values, attention math,
  kernel code, or unrelated dispatch logic.
- Applied ONLY to the PR arm source tree. The Main arm is untouched.

Applied to: python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/decode_attention.py
Base revision: 3fdf6f7318364c1b09398aea4d947ed633ac9eca

--- a/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/decode_attention.py
+++ b/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/decode_attention.py
@@ -41,3 +41,10 @@
 _is_hip = is_hip()
 _is_gfx1250 = _is_hip and is_gfx1250_supported()
 _is_gfx115 = _is_hip and is_gfx115_supported()
+# gfx1100-validation (local, temporary): additionally accept exactly gfx1100 so
+# the grouped GQA decode launch config can be measured on RDNA3.0 (W7900).
+_is_gfx1100_validation = torch.cuda.is_available() and (
+    torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).gcnArchName.startswith("gfx1100")
+)
+_is_gfx115 = _is_hip and (is_gfx115_supported() or _is_gfx1100_validation)
